# Rewrite Prompt (RP)

When a user message starts with **RP** (or clearly says “rewrite prompt”), do **not** execute the task yet.

## What to do

1. **Read the rough prompt** — treat everything after `RP` as the draft intent.
2. **Ground in the codebase** — skim the relevant project files, fliers, samples, guides, registry, sizes, and prior patterns so the rewrite matches how this studio actually works.
3. **Decide: one prompt or batches**
   - **Single prompt** — small, one-agent scope (one bugfix, one layout tweak, one file family).
   - **Batches** — default when the draft spans multiple systems, has several independent goals, or would overwhelm one model (routing + API + UI + auth + docs, etc.). Split into **ordered, self-contained** prompts a different AI can run one-at-a-time.
4. **Each prompt must be comprehensive and runnable alone** — include:
   - Goal / intent in one line
   - Prerequisites / depends on (e.g. “Requires Batch 1 merged”)
   - Constraints (brand vs standalone, size/platform, do/don’t)
   - Exact paths, ids, and files to touch when known
   - Acceptance criteria / hand-off
5. **Hand back only copyable text**
   - **One prompt:** reply body is only that prompt.
   - **Batches:** reply body is only the batch prompts. Label each with a single line `Batch N/M — <short title>` then the prompt. No preamble, no “here’s a rewrite”, no closing offers. Put dependency notes inside each batch prompt, not in surrounding commentary.
6. **Batching rules**
   - Prefer vertical slices that leave the app working after each batch when possible.
   - Order by dependency (API/routes before UI that consumes them; route moves before link rewrites; public page before auth return-URL polish).
   - Keep each batch simple and direct — one clear job.
   - If the user pastes multiple unrelated tasks in one RP, emit one batch (or one prompt) per task, still ordered if any depend on each other.
   - Do not invent scope the draft did not imply; if a batch needs a choice, encode it inside that batch as an explicit option.

## Do not

- Start coding, committing, or “just doing it” on an RP message unless they explicitly say to implement after the rewrite.
- Invent brand assets, sizes, or Emergence placement the draft did not imply — encode those choices as explicit options inside the prompt if unclear.
- Wrap prompts in commentary the user has to strip before pasting.
- Dump one mega-prompt when the work clearly needs multiple models/batches.
